{%- comment -%}
  The one "is this a foam bed the foam guarantee covers?" test, shared by
  everything that makes a foam-specific claim about a product: the foam
  guarantee line and per-night price (buy box, cards, finder result via
  Lunova.foamBed), the foam tagline fallback, the cost reframe, the
  mechanism diagram and the comparison table.

  A word like "orthopaedic" in a title, type or tag is not evidence of a
  guarantee (egg-crate beds, car seats and nest beds carry it too), so the
  test reads what the product itself promises:
    1. tag "guarantee:no"  → never (wins over everything)
    2. tag "guarantee:yes" → always
    3. not a bed           → never: the product type's first part (before
                             " > ") doesn't mention "bed" ("Dog Houses > …"),
                             or it's a car seat (tag "dog car seat" /
                             "car seat", or "car seat" in the title)
    4. its description promises it: contains "no-flatten guarantee"
  Anything else → not covered. Tag a product guarantee:yes when its
  description words the guarantee differently.

  Output: the word "true" when covered, nothing otherwise. Capture it:
    {%- capture is_foam -%}{%- render 'foam-bed', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- if is_foam == 'true' -%} … {%- endif -%}

  Keep in step with Lunova.foamBed() in assets/global.js and the finder's
  product JSON (snippets/finder-product-json).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  if product != blank
    assign fb_tags = product.tags | join: ',' | downcase | prepend: ',' | append: ','
    assign fb_ok = false
    if fb_tags contains ',guarantee:no,'
      assign fb_ok = false
    elsif fb_tags contains ',guarantee:yes,'
      assign fb_ok = true
    else
      assign fb_bed = true
      assign fb_type = product.type | default: '' | downcase | strip
      assign fb_first = fb_type | split: '>' | first | default: '' | strip
      if fb_first != ''
        unless fb_first contains 'bed'
          assign fb_bed = false
        endunless
      endif
      assign fb_title = product.title | default: '' | downcase
      if fb_tags contains ',dog car seat,' or fb_tags contains ',car seat,' or fb_title contains 'car seat'
        assign fb_bed = false
      endif
      if fb_bed
        assign fb_desc = product.description | default: '' | downcase
        if fb_desc contains 'no-flatten guarantee' or fb_desc contains 'no flatten guarantee'
          assign fb_ok = true
        endif
      endif
    endif
    if fb_ok
      echo 'true'
    endif
  endif
-%}
